def table(findings):
    s='| # | Severity | Scene / location | Finding and learner question | Concrete repair |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n'
    for i,(sev,loc,title,why,fix) in enumerate(findings,1):
        s+=f'| {i} | {sev} | {loc} | **{title}** {why} | {fix} |\n'
    return s

for key,findings in L.items():
    q,trace,overlap=TRACE[key]; d=A['designs'][key]
    counts={sev:sum(f[0]==sev for f in findings) for sev in ['blocker','should fix','optional']}
    text=f'# {key}: independent student learning review\n\nReviewed 30 October 2026 by Codex. Design Revision 1. Source: `{d["path"]}`. SHA-256: `{d["sha256"]}`.\n\nInspected the written proposal, narration, visual plans, attempts, feedback, notes and metadata. Earlier lesson sources were compared for prerequisite and double-teaching checks. This is a proposal review. It does not establish plate fit, playback motion, caption fit or human listening. No real student explanations were collected. Repeat on the exact voiced preview before export.\n\nMain learner question: **{q}**\n\n## Findings\n\n'+table(findings)
    text+=f'\n**Counts: {counts["blocker"]} blocker, {counts["should fix"]} should fix, {counts["optional"]} optional.** Counts overlap the science review where the same issue affects learning; do not add the two counts as distinct repairs.\n\n## Learner trace and boundaries\n\n{trace}\n\n{overlap}\n\n## Arithmetic and reading load\n\n{NUM[key]}\n\nRecount: {d["narrationCharacters"]:,} narration characters in {len(d["scenes"])} scenes. The source contains {d["emDashCount"]} em dashes. Counts use normalized line endings, lines beginning `> `, joined within each scene, and removed bold markers. Full per-scene counts and exact source hashes are in `../assets/brief118-source-audit.json`.\n\nThe current-case layout, dimmed previous work and retained question cards are useful. Every question specifies a visible ten-second countdown after speech. Feedback contains a crossed classic mistake; its exact duration is untested. Optional notes have a quiet copy/pause hold. The plan uses organisms, apparatus or data rather than text substitutes. Continuous motion has not been inspected at playback speed, so no motion pass is claimed.\n\n## Timing and verdict\n\n'
    if key in ['m8c06','m8p05c','m8b09','m8b11']:
        text+='The design is already about 568-570 seconds. Repairs above replace existing clauses or screen labels; no new scene or hold is required. Named cuts are given where longer wording is suggested. Recount and time the exact speech after author resolution. '
    text+=('Resolve the blockers before recording. ' if counts['blocker'] else 'Resolve the should-fix findings before recording. ')
    text+='Retain the successful visual comparisons and approved lesson boundary. Science review remains separate; neither this source review nor art QA approves a recording or release.\n\n## Resolution\n'
    (PM/'checks'/f'{key}-learning-review.md').write_text(polish(text),encoding='utf8')

