for key,findings in S.items():
    d=A['designs'][key]; subject,quote,note=SYLL[key]
    counts={sev:sum(f[0]==sev for f in findings) for sev in ['blocker','should fix','optional']}
    txt=f'# {key}: independent science check\n\nChecked 30 October 2026 by Codex, against Revision 1. Source SHA-256: `{d["sha256"]}`. All narration lines, planned on-screen copy, attempts, feedback, notes, number lists and metadata were inspected. This is a source review; no laboratory experiment, voiced preview, full playback or human listening pass is claimed.\n\n## Findings\n\n| # | Severity | Location | Problem | Repair and source |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n'
    for i,(sev,loc,problem,repair) in enumerate(findings,1): txt+=f'| {i} | {sev} | {loc} | {problem} | {repair} |\n'
    txt+=f'\n**Counts: {counts["blocker"]} blocker, {counts["should fix"]} should fix.** These overlap the learning review where they concern the same repair.\n\n## Exact syllabus check\n\n'+quote+'\n\n'+note
    txt+=f' The official 2017 DOCX paragraph extract was checked word for word against the local syllabus ledger and design quotation. Source SHA-256: `{A["syllabus"][subject]["sourceSha256"]}`; extract path: `{A["syllabus"][subject]["extractPath"]}`. Relevant paragraphs are recorded in `../assets/brief118-source-audit.json`. The Chemistry extraction contains U+FFFD for some dash glyphs, so it establishes the words and list but cannot independently certify that dash character. No substitution of 2025 syllabus content was made. [Official course page](https://www.nsw.gov.au/education-and-training/nesa/curriculum/science/{"chemistry" if subject=="chem" else "biology"}-stage-6-2017).\n\n## Fact and figure checks\n\n'+VERIFY[key]
    txt+='\n\n## Recalculation\n\n'+NUM[key]
    txt+=f'\n\nNarration recount: {d["narrationCharacters"]:,} characters, {len(d["scenes"])} scenes; U+2014 count {d["emDashCount"]}. No numerical or chemical spelling change was made to a source lesson. Exact scenes and counts are retained in the source audit.\n\n## Site-error decisions\n\nRead-only HTML was checked, with file hashes and normalized full text retained in `../assets/brief118-source-audit.json`. Confirmed new rows, and rejected or unresolved author suggestions, are in `../assets/brief118-site-corrections-proposed.md`. That file is for root integration; this review does not change the site or shared log. Missing source support is labelled unresolved rather than asserted false.\n\n## Remaining checks\n\nResolve the numbered findings before recording. Exact procedural colour timing, current mixture SDSs, missing annual dataset rows and dash glyph certification remain open where stated. Question wording is HSC-style; originality against every historical exam has not been exhaustively established. Check the revised source, then the exact voiced preview for learning, timing, motion and captions. Human listening and release approval remain pending.\n\n## Resolution\n'
    if subject=='bio':
        txt=txt.replace('The Chemistry extraction contains U+FFFD for some dash glyphs, so it establishes the words and list but cannot independently certify that dash character. ','')
    (PM/'checks'/f'{key}-claude-science-check.md').write_text(polish(txt),encoding='utf8')

